ush rates up in the short term rather than down; his key advice for rate-sensitive industries is to watch the data, not the stock market. Masters of Scale Masters of Scale Chicago Fed President on inflation, recession, and Trump’s attacks Inflation expectations Federal Reserve Interest rates AI bubble Productivity Macro decisions Forward guidance Core inflation Unanchoring of inflation expectations Stagflation Lump of labor fallacy FOMC\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-masterscale-通胀预期失锚-美联储最怕的不是关税/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://content.production.cdn.art19.com/images/71/5b/8e/71/715b8e71-0bdf-42d3-bd31-bd55674c74b8/b6a1944de87c528e7b186c22cb1583d6816630a375675e194f6abe4b98ac796808b5b96d4827d496c2bba16d5a00895be2616c9ef2de840178324bbbdd2c658e.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"M\"><span class=\"dur\">35:42</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Masters of Scale</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>What the Fed fears most is not tariffs but unanchored inflation expectations</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Chicago Fed President Goolsbee identifies the biggest risk as inflation: after five and a half years above target, the AI narrative may push rates up in the short term rather than down; his key advice for rate-sensitive industries is to watch the data, not the stock market.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Inflation expectations</span><span class=\"tag\">Federal Reserve</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Sunscreen Toxicity Myth Debunked: Entering Blood Isn&#x27;t Harmful, but Vitamin D Risk Is Real The most-cited evidence for &#x27;sunscreen is toxic and causes cancer&#x27; mostly involves absurd doses or reversed causality; chemical sunscreen entering the blood doesn&#x27;t equal toxicity. But daily application does increase the risk of vitamin D deficiency in winter, and evidence for preventing melanoma in darker skin is especially weak. Science Vs Science Vs Sunscreen: Could It Be Toxic?? sunscreen vitamin D melanoma chemical sunscreen evidence-based medicine skin cancer oxybenzone UV index Fitzpatrick scale SPF mineral sunscreen RCT\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-sciencevs-防晒霜不是毒药-但深肤色人群可能真不用防黑素瘤/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/f521b120-2c30-11e6-b5f3-63ee984ee1a4/image/e7470287efbfa0aff068175bb6c31805.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">50:52</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Science Vs</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>Sunscreen Toxicity Myth Debunked: Entering Blood Isn&#x27;t Harmful, but Vitamin D Risk Is Real</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The most-cited evidence for &#x27;sunscreen is toxic and causes cancer&#x27; mostly involves absurd doses or reversed causality; chemical sunscreen entering the blood doesn&#x27;t equal toxicity. But daily application does increase the risk of vitamin D deficiency in winter, and evidence for preventing melanoma in darker skin is especially weak.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">sunscreen</span><span class=\"tag\">vitamin D</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Without Plate Tectonics, No Life: Earth Is a Lucky Planet Plate tectonics reshapes the Earth&#x27;s surface at the speed of fingernail growth, creating and destroying about 3 square kilometers of oceanic crust each year; it alters climate, isolates species, and even determines whether life exists—without it, there would be no life. In Our Time In Our Time Archive: Plate Tectonics Plate Tectonics Earth Science Origin of Life Scientific Revolution Gaia Theory Planetary Habitability Benioff zone seafloor spreading Vine–Matthews hypothesis mantle plume black smoker Gaia theory\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-inourtime-没有板块构造就没有生命-地球是幸运的行星/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/images/ic/400x400/p0m1q0p7.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">44:27</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">In Our Time</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>Without Plate Tectonics, No Life: Earth Is a Lucky Planet</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Plate tectonics reshapes the Earth&#x27;s surface at the speed of fingernail growth, creating and destroying about 3 square kilometers of oceanic crust each year; it alters climate, isolates species, and even determines whether life exists—without it, there would be no life.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Plate Tectonics</span><span class=\"tag\">Earth Science</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Ketosis for Mental Illness: It&#x27;s Not About Weight Loss, It&#x27;s Mitochondria Psychiatrist Chris Palmer uses ketogenic and low-carb diets to help patients with treatment-resistant mental illness find relief; the key isn&#x27;t just weight loss but changing brain energy metabolism and neurotransmitters through mitophagy and biogenesis. Huberman Lab Huberman Lab Essentials: Diet &amp; Nutrition for Mental Health | Dr. Chris Palmer ketogenic diet mental health mitochondria low-carb clinical cases Mitophagy Mitochondrial biogenesis Ketosis Schizoaffective disorder\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-huberman-生酮饮食治疗难治性精神疾病-线粒体是核心/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"http